<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33988" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">partŭrītĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		parturio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a desiring to bring forth</i>, <i>labor</i>, <i>travail</i> (late Lat.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Hier. adv.
				Jovin. 1</span></i>, n. 22.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a bearing</i> or
				<i>bringing forth</i>, <i>parturition</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">novae vitae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aug. Conf. 8, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cordis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Ep. 34</span></i>
			 (al. 31).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>Any grievous pains</i>: inferni, Capreol. Epist. ad
			Vital. et Const.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
